  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $\\frac{1}{5-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,5)\\cup (5,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of ${t}^{8}-3$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of ${e}^{1-t}$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14094319/assets/74064710fbc274a0ff9ebc284891333ef9521c0c69d020e7c5e3a7d469784e23.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,5)\\cup (5,\\infty ).$",
